# One checkout, three operating systems.
#
# The engine is developed on Windows and compiled on macOS CI, and
# scripts/build.mjs verifies that every core file is inlined into the fixture
# byte-for-byte. Nothing here breaks on CRLF today — the comparison happens
# in memory, on data read from a single disk — but a line ending that differs
# between two machines is exactly the kind of thing that turns into a mystery
# failure in the one place it cannot be debugged, which is CI. So pin it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` stores and checks out LF
# for everything it decides is text, which is what every tool here expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary or generated content: leave completely alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ipa binary
*.xcuserstate binary
